# ProgramOS instance settings.
#
# HOW SETTINGS ARE READ (two ways; this matters):
#   1. Keys in PART 1 are read from the file `.env` in the repo root.
#   2. Keys in PART 2 are read ONLY from the process environment. A line in
#      `.env` does nothing for them. Export them in the service definition
#      (systemd `Environment=`, pm2 `env`, or your shell before `node dist/index.js`).
# The parser does NOT strip inline comments. Put nothing after a value.
# Never commit `.env`.

# ============ PART 1: goes in `.env` ============

# REQUIRED. The bot's name. The code default is the upstream framework's
# default name, not "Coordinator".
ASSISTANT_NAME=Coordinator
# REQUIRED. The address the bot sends from and replies to.
SEND_FROM_EMAIL=
SEND_FROM_NAME=Coordinator
# The operator's address for host mail copies.
OPERATOR_CC_EMAIL=
TZ=America/Chicago

# Identity (src/instance-identity.ts). Each default is this repo's
# placeholder, so set all four for a real deployment. A malformed value stops
# the host at startup. With a real program repo, so does a missing or
# placeholder INSTITUTION_DOMAIN or ADMIN_AUTHOR_EMAILS
# (src/identity-settings-check.ts). Lower case; no quotes needed.
# REQUIRED for a real program repo: the host refuses to start when this is
# empty or example.edu.
# Your institution's mail domain. A blocked sender on this domain gets one
# "access closed" reply, and a route named in an allowlist row resolves to
# <name>@<this domain>.
INSTITUTION_DOMAIN=
# The bot's own mail domain: the default bot address (program@<domain>, used
# when SEND_FROM_EMAIL is empty), the Message-ID domain of outbound mail, and
# the bot's git author (program-bot@<domain>). The prompts in groups/ and the
# skills in container/skills/ also name that git author as text; change them
# to match.
BOT_MAIL_DOMAIN=
# The git author email of your inbound mail intake service. It must equal the
# author on that service's commits exactly. An original .eml is accepted only
# when this author first committed it.
INTAKE_GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL=
# REQUIRED for a real program repo. The admin's git author emails, separated
# by commas: the only identities allowed to change the protected governance
# files. This list replaces the placeholder list. With a real program repo
# (PROGRAM_ORIGIN_PATTERN is set, or the origin of the checkout or the read
# mirror is not example-org/program-repo) the host refuses to start when this
# is empty or names a placeholder address.
ADMIN_AUTHOR_EMAILS=

# REQUIRED. Shared secret for inbound mail webhooks.
WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# Model credentials for the agent (through the host's credential proxy).
# Use ONE of the first two. Leave unused lines out of `.env` entirely.
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Optional: an approved endpoint that serves Claude, for the AGENT only.
# The reply sensor does NOT use this setting; see BEHAVIOUR_SENSOR_DISABLED.
# Only the host and port are used. A path prefix in this URL is dropped, so
# the endpoint must serve /v1/messages at the root of its host.
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=

# Outbound mail provider (the reference deployment's provider).
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# Signing secret of the provider's events webhook (starts with whsec_).
# Endpoint: https://<your-host>/resend/webhook, subscribed to email.delivered,
# email.bounced, email.complained and email.failed. Read from `.env` only.
# Without it the route answers 503 and bounces are not reported.
# Steps: AGENTS.md, "Webhooks from other services".
# RESEND_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# Telegram. Optional as a channel for the team, but operator alerts
# (delivery failures, routed-approval notices) are sent to the admin here.
# Without a token those alerts are not delivered.
# Create the chat sender allowlist first (copy
# config-examples/sender-allowlist.json to ~/.config/nanoclaw/): if that file
# is missing or invalid, the chat trigger check allows no sender.
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
# TELEGRAM_ADMIN_CHAT_ID=

# Web chat (optional).
# WEBCHAT_SECRET=

# Optional features.
# Secret of the push webhook on the PROGRAM repo (GitHub: Settings, Webhooks).
# Payload URL https://<your-host>/api/github-push, content type
# application/json, the push event only. Choose a long random value and enter
# the same value in GitHub. Read from `.env` first, then the process
# environment. Without it the route answers 503, direct commits get no audit
# entry and the protected-file tripwire does not run.
# Steps: AGENTS.md, "Webhooks from other services".
# GITHUB_PUSH_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# EMAIL_OUTREACH_TASK_ID=
# DEAD_LETTER_ALERT_JID=
# OUTREACH_SUMMARY_JID=
# OUTBOUND_EMAIL_STAGGER_MS=

# ============ PART 2: export in the process environment ============

# REQUIRED. Absolute path to the program repo checkout on this host.
# PROGRAM_REPO=/srv/repos/your-program-repo
# Optional bare mirror for pinned host reads.
# PROGRAM_READ_MIRROR=
# REQUIRED if your program repo is not the placeholder one: a regular
# expression that the repo's git origin URL must match.
# PROGRAM_ORIGIN_PATTERN=^git@github\.com:your-org/your-program-repo(\.git)?$
# Any git host works, including GitHub Enterprise on your institution's own
# host name. When this is set, the URL is checked against the pattern only,
# so keep ^ and $. A GitHub Enterprise host, with the dots written as [.]:
# PROGRAM_ORIGIN_PATTERN=^git@git[.]example[.]edu:your-org/your-program-repo([.]git)?$
# For an HTTPS origin, with or without a token in the URL:
# PROGRAM_ORIGIN_PATTERN=^https://([^@/?#\s]+@)?git[.]example[.]edu/your-org/your-program-repo([.]git)?$

# Keep the listener on loopback and put a reverse proxy in front.
# The code default is all interfaces.
# WEBHOOK_HOST=127.0.0.1
# WEBHOOK_PORT=3003
# CREDENTIAL_PROXY_PORT=3001

# The reply sensor calls the model provider's public API directly, with its
# own key, and sends reply text and knowledge-base excerpts. It ignores
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL. Keep it off unless that destination is approved for
# your data.
# BEHAVIOUR_SENSOR_DISABLED=1
# SENSOR_MODEL=

# NANOCLAW_AGENT_MODEL=
# NANOCLAW_GATE_MODEL=
# NANOCLAW_AGENT_EFFORT=
# EMAIL_SENDER_DAILY_CAP=
# EMAIL_PERSON_SENDER_DAILY_CAP=
